{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJVVVv3cyuLYaD6vLdu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `slugify` in `slug.js`: `'Crème Brûlée'` now gives `'creme-brulee'`, and `npm test` passes all 3 tests.\n\nThe cause was that the regex replaced every character outside `a-z0-9`, so accented letters were turned into dashes. The function now strips accents first, by decomposing each letter with `normalize('NFD')` and removing the combining marks, so `è` becomes `e`.\n\nI also made it trim leading and trailing dashes. The comment at the top of the file already promised that, but the code didn't do it.\n\nIn `test/slug.test.js` I added a test for the accent case and one for dash trimming.\n\nLetters with no accent-style decomposition, such as `ß`, `ø` and `æ`, are still dropped. I didn't add special handling for them, so say if you want it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":23721,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":232},"output_tokens":272,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ca6f0f5-4edd-4cca-8ff2-e556d9d1bb3a","uuid":"adf053e6-3bfe-4af6-b344-7819be60e78c","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:28:00.616Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJVVLkAkpJ4eUcYizE6"}
